{
  "name": "Pyramid",
  "family": "Pyramid",
  "description": "**Goal:** clear the whole 28-card **pyramid**.\n\n- Remove cards in **pairs that total 13** (A=1 … Q=12): drag a card **onto its partner** and both go to the **discard**. A **King** (13) goes to the discard alone.\n- A card can be played only once the **two cards overlapping it from below** are gone, so a card can't pair with one that covers it. The base row is free to start, and the rest open up as you clear toward the apex.\n- The **stock's** top card is face up and playable; drag it to the **waste** to set it aside, where it never pairs. The waste's top card stays playable: to pair it with the stock's top card, drop it onto the stock.\n- When the stock runs out, **tap it** to turn the waste back over. You get **three passes** through the stock in all.\n- The game is lost when no move is left. Your **score** is the number of pyramid cards removed, 28 for a win.\n- _Tip: the **Scarab** deck shows a small gold hint on each card — the rank it pairs with to reach 13._",
  "rules": {
    "tableau": {
      "single": true,
      "seedNone": true,
      "when": "card.value + top.value == 13 && all(c in coveredBy(depot), c != source && empty(c))",
      "reason": "Pair cards that total 13"
    }
  },
  "depots": [
